    "created_at": "2025-07-18T08:21:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-18T08:21:45Z",
    "body": "If we keep it in table it's only going to be a little weird if you manually do something and then also decide to inspect `code`. That seems okay? (And that's likely legacy code that probably does expect it to return the correct code.)\r\n\r\nI think that still makes this cleanly disconnected overall, as what code you get is a function of the legacy table and your name only.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
