    "created_at": "2025-07-19T02:23:52Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-19T02:23:52Z",
    "body": "Sure, but it makes new exceptions that happen to have the same names as legacy ones get legacy baggage.\r\n\r\nAnyway, I'm still unsure where this leaves us. Do you object to how Chromium's shipped this, such that WebKit does not support merging this unless Chromium does another shipping cycle to add back code? I don't think we'll prioritize that very highly, but we could do it after WebKit and Gecko do. Or would you prefer to merge this, and work on getting multi-implementer interest for adding the code behavior afterward?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
